            "target_entity_instance": "endogenous, bottom-up building sector",
            "target_entity_type": "PhysicalFeature",
            "paragraph": "In modeling cooling energy consumption (Eq. (10)), GCAM and other IAMs share a focus on incorporating climatic variables, building characteristics, and socioeconomic factors, yet they differ in approach and assumptions. GCAM features an endogenous, bottom-up building sector that directly models these influences within a single framework, while other IAMs, such as AIM-Hub and MESSAGEix models, tend to rely on multi-model coupling and AC adoption assumptions to represent cooling energy demand.",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
